{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff","id":1509154,"title":"An antediluvian Caitiff...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-21T03:04:48-07:00","id":1509154,"title":"An antediluvian Caitiff...","content":"Several sources tell us that Vitae grows thicker and more powerful with time... a LOT of time, so there are no hard and fast rules for this.<br /> I was asking myself: what's the extreme limit of this process?<br /> <br /> Let's say the Malkavian Antediluvian wakes up bored one night and decide to embrace a random guy, then make him Embrace someone else and so on to the extreme limit. Usually that limit, in ancient times, would be the 13th generation but let's say that after 100 failed attempts or so, Malkav gets a 14th generation Caitiff.<br /> Under his vigilant eye the Caitiff neither is destroyed nor he commits Diablerie, so he grows older, and older, and older.<br /> <br /> After more or less 20.000 years ( modern time ) what could that weird creature become?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T03:14:16-07:00","id":1509156,"title":"","content":"With the information we have about the antediluvians in the book of Gehenna, by that time he would have already become a very powerful creature, but still relatively weaker than the other third generation, but just like them he is capable of developing a hatred or just be weary, in some Gehenna scenarios after reaching full power the antediluvians just stopped, they have the power to do whatever they want but simply do nothing, total apathy, but I don't think that's what you want to know, what I suppose is that over time he ceases to be a Caitiff and becomes an independent clan with his own characteristics and maybe even a unique discipline or as his blood grows stronger, he develops the curse of the Malkav and becomes one of them or even a variant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T03:22:59-07:00","id":1509157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff#post1509154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several sources tell us that Vitae grows thicker and more powerful with time... a LOT of time, so there are no hard and fast rules for this.<br /> I was asking myself: what's the extreme limit of this process?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because this is the oldest cover story vampires use to pretend they Didn't commit diablerie. Assuming you aren't talking about V5's blood potency mechanic of course, but that outlines how it works in the rules.<br /> <br /> Every other edition &quot;Blood Thickening&quot; is a lie, vampire's need diablerie or direct magical intervention to Simulate diablerie(like the &quot;from marduke's throat&quot;) to rise in generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T03:28:50-07:00","id":1509158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff#post1509154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several sources tell us that Vitae grows thicker and more powerful with time... a LOT of time, so there are no hard and fast rules for this.<br /> I was asking myself: what's the extreme limit of this process?</div> </div> </div> </div>In regard to this issue I consider it that additional requirements, factors, occurances, decisions, and tendencies definitely need to be included.<br /> <br /> For example in regard to a Vampiress or a Vamprie becoming more powerful and capable in a general, overall, or standard way ( or for instance developing her or his innate, basic, and natural undead and vampiric powers and abilties ) , the process and events should be linked to and relative to some distinct qualities, phenomenons, and choices.<br /> Among these certainly could be included for example : personal achievements, definition and participation within teams or groups, subjective and inner ideas and ruminations, and finished or accomplished quests, interests, and activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T09:47:01-07:00","id":1509204,"title":"","content":"We do have some really old &amp; potent caitiff that could become the founders of there own clans such as Emmlich the Mad and the Monitor of Istanbul if there willing to take the next steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T11:47:33-07:00","id":1509221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1509157#post1509157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, because this is the oldest cover story vampires use to pretend they Didn't commit diablerie. Assuming you aren't talking about V5's blood potency mechanic of course, but that outlines how it works in the rules.<br /> <br /> Every other edition &quot;Blood Thickening&quot; is a lie, vampire's need diablerie or direct magical intervention to Simulate diablerie(like the &quot;from marduke's throat&quot;) to rise in generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. In the Dark ages 12th gen could be thin blooded and unable to sire. By the time of the modern nights that no longer seemed the case and it requred 13th gen or below to be a thin blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T13:00:08-07:00","id":1509227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1509221#post1509221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not entirely. In the Dark ages 12th gen could be thin blooded and unable to sire. By the time of the modern nights that no longer seemed the case and it requred 13th gen or below to be a thin blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit different than when vampires claim they raised in generation.<br /> <br /> A 12th gen from dark ages still has the same blood per turn limits, blood buff limits, and discipline limits as they did in the dark ages, they just lost the &quot;thin blood&quot; flaw.<br /> <br /> To show my point, look at the 16th gen thin bloods in Becket's Jyhad Diary. They have even Lower caps than the 12th-to-15th gen had at their worst despite them &quot;Thickening&quot;. Generation limits stay the same, &quot;thin blood&quot; is just an additional flaw (and it Still appears among higher gens sometimes. You can have methuselas with the thin blooded flaw, it's basically vampire hemophilia).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 04-21-2023, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T13:36:36-07:00","id":1509230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A 12th gen from dark ages still has the same blood per turn limits, blood buff limits, and discipline limits as they did in the dark ages, they just lost the &quot;thin blood&quot; flaw </div> </div> </div>In just 800 years or so!<br /> Now, let's make them 20.000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T23:20:41-07:00","id":1509257,"title":"","content":"The problem is that Lore As Written is extremely inconsistent. Originally, Generation was a fixed parameter from 1st to 13th and there was no &quot;thickening of the blood&quot; whatsoever, which tied up with the theme of cannibalism as the way vampires obtain power and break their glass ceiling.<br /> At some point they released Time of Thin Blood, with extended the generational limit to 15th in just a matter of decades and Dark Age, which reduced it to 12 Generations and gave an approximate time frame of 800 years. Was there an upper limit before that?<br /> We don't know, but I have ruled in my current game that 12th generation kindred could not be Sired until the last times of the Roman Empire.<br /> So, what's the reason given for this? Time of Thin Blood had it easy, as they could pin it all on impending Gehenna and forget about it. An explanation for what happened during the Dark Ages is harder to find, and at some point this idea of &quot;Thickening&quot; came up. The problem is that, mechanically, there is no evidence for this. A Dark Ages 7th generation is mechanically the same as a Time of Judgement one.<br /> So, at the end of the night you will have to make up your own call. Does Generation mechanically improve every X years? Is the increment evenly distributed or are the intervals getting increasingly shorter?<br /> Maybe it doesn't. A 7th Generation will always have a 20 Max Blood Pool and 6 Max dots and so on. But for some reason younger Generations could not Embrace I'm the past, but now can. Does it mean that the First has to wait for millennia until he could create the 2nd Generation? Once again, what's the rythym of this process?<br /> Personally I haven't found a 100% consistent answer and toyed with different versions depending on the themes I want to introduce in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T16:52:40-07:00","id":1509536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1509257#post1509257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that Lore As Written is extremely inconsistent...</div> </div> </div> </div>It remains somewhat consistent if you think of the bloods ability to create higher and higher generations over time as something separate from &quot;thickening&quot; in the sense of vampires changing gen just from age.<br /> <br /> As you said, a 7th gen vampire is mechanically the same between dark ages and modern nights. Current Gens after 12th are Weaker than the 12th gens were in dark ages. This aspect of generation remains consistent.<br /> <br /> Vampires going up in Gen is clearly not what's happening, the ability of the vampiric curse to Spread is what's getting stronger while individual vampires remain the same.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking, this has a hard-cap. Specifically, at either 17th gen(1 dot max disciplines, usable blood pool of 2 with 8 reserved for raising only. basically indistinguishable from a ghoul or dhampir) or 18th(0 dot discipline max, no usable blood pool) it becomes physically impossible for an even higher gen vampire to be made because they'd be mechanically incapable of existing(-1 discipline limit makes no sense and usable blood pool can't shrink any further).<br /> <br /> This actually raises the interesting idea that <i>Maybe</i>, the time of thin blood hasn't happened yet. Even by the time of Becket's Jyhad Diary, the brand new gen is 16th. Vampires still have at least 2 generations of &quot;thinbloods&quot; to go before they reach the true limit and the curse can no longer progress and embracing further becomes truly impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T02:52:47-07:00","id":1509566,"title":"","content":"Mabye the thickening of the Blood, while not changing the overall Generation, could still apport some change and benefits ( slightly increased Blood Pool, raised maximum cap in a single attribute or discipline ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T10:17:54-07:00","id":1509595,"title":"","content":"A very old caitiff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T06:28:57-07:00","id":1509710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff#post1509154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several sources tell us that Vitae grows thicker and more powerful with time... a LOT of time, so there are no hard and fast rules for this.<br /> I was asking myself: what's the extreme limit of this process?<br /> <br /> Let's say the Malkavian Antediluvian wakes up bored one night and decide to embrace a random guy, then make him Embrace someone else and so on to the extreme limit. Usually that limit, in ancient times, would be the 13th generation but let's say that after 100 failed attempts or so, Malkav gets a 14th generation Caitiff.<br /> Under his vigilant eye the Caitiff neither is destroyed nor he commits Diablerie, so he grows older, and older, and older.<br /> <br /> After more or less 20.000 years ( modern time ) what could that weird creature become?</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 has kind of broken the lore here (blood potency makes absolutely no sense in the context of masquerade's lore) but in general, it's not the individual vampire's blood that thickens, it's the whole generation's. Effectively, the more of a generation exist, and the longer, the more the blood stabilises enough to get you to embrace capacity and, possibly, to get you to lose the Thin Blood flaw. Assuming said Caitiff was subject to the Generation Curse (see Caine's dictum that each generation is weaker than the last) that caitiff would still be limited to 4 discipline dots and 5 dots of traits, as well as a terrible blood pool. If they weren't subject to Caine's Curse for some insane reason I cannot fathom, then they would be exactly as powerful as an Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, barring Golconda, they'd probably be the only Cainite with every discipline (the EXP has to go somewhere) but still limited to 4s. Having a weak beast (due to 14th gen) would also allow them to retain more of who they were when mortal. With Golconda they could have unlimited discipline dots, but still have a very limited blood pool. They'd also probably be the nicest cainite ever, in Golconda for 8000 years or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12911,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","user":"Lateral.Psychotropy","date":".  Clarifications 04-26-2023, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T07:09:27-07:00","id":1509715,"title":"","content":"I thought we where going to be talking about 'The Stoneman' that caitiff in the Outcast Book.<br /> <br /> The problem with 'The Thickening of Blood' is that the phase doesn't really mean anything both mechanically or really lorewise. My personal interpretation is that 'The Thickening of Blood' is the in character explanation of how players can get more powerful then NPC characters much 'quicker' in them getting XP to get their stats up.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T14:44:44-07:00","id":1509784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1509715#post1509715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought we where going to be talking about 'The Stoneman' that caitiff in the Outcast Book.<br /> <br /> The problem with 'The Thickening of Blood' is that the phase doesn't really mean anything both mechanically or really lorewise. My personal interpretation is that 'The Thickening of Blood' is the in character explanation of how players can get more powerful then NPC characters much 'quicker' in them getting XP to get their stats up.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what? It absolutely does! Dark ages, 13th gen can't embrace. You get a lot of them, the blood thickens, they can. Same with 15th (we have a <b>lot</b> of thin-bloods) now siring the 16th (see Becket's Jihad Diary).<br /> <br /> If you just go by XP, then it's when it doesn't make sense, because a character in torpor gains nothing, but their blood should thicken (as it's supposed to be time related) with the passage of the years.<br /> <br /> ...Okay, I might be too passionate about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T15:12:58-07:00","id":1509788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lateral.Psychotropy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1509784#post1509784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait what? It absolutely does! Dark ages, 13th gen can't embrace. You get a lot of them, the blood thickens, they can. Same with 15th (we have a <b>lot</b> of thin-bloods) now siring the 16th (see Becket's Jihad Diary).<br /> <br /> If you just go by XP, then it's when it doesn't make sense, because a character in torpor gains nothing, but their blood should thicken (as it's supposed to be time related) with the passage of the years.<br /> <br /> ...Okay, I might be too passionate about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that they <b>can't</b> embrace it's that they have a low chance to have a successful embrace. In the text of the book talking about Thin Blooded it says this:<br /> <br /> &quot;It is possible, I\u2019m told, for the youngest of us to create a vampire themselves, but it is rare as few of you have the strength to do the act, physical or political. Without the physical power, the victim simply dies. Without the political power, some angry elder kills you both for the having the audacity to try it. We don\u2019t tend to bother counting Generation after the Twelfth, as anything further removed from Caine can scarcely be called a vampire at all. Tragic wretches, one and all. We call them Thin Blooded and watch for signs that they need to be put down.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also in the same Dark Ages book it says this about thickening blood.<br /> <br /> &quot;I\u2019ve heard that given enough age, the blood thickens, no matter how close to Caine your sire was, you can grow to have blood like ice and a beast as terrible as a burning, lightless sun. This, of course, is rumor and hearsay. Nothing to concern yourself with too greatly.&quot;\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> &quot;There is, I\u2019m afraid, one way that your blood may be thickened, but it\u2019s a terrible, and unforgivable sin. If we are sin in flesh, then this is the thing that even the wickedest of us shies from. I would rather not tell you about it; I dread to say the word out loud. But it is vital you know about it so that you remain very careful who you let close to you and when. This most vile act we call the Amaranth, and to commit it is to drink the blood of another vampire. But not just his blood, the whole of him, even drinking his soul and destroying all that he ever was so that you can rob him of his power and increase your own. Make no mistake, it is not a thing you can do by accident, and even if you found yourself needing to drain another of your kind to unconsciousness, there is still a chance to turn back and leave him in torpor or ashes, which is better than the alternative. Believe me. If you so will it, if you push through your mind and sanity, resist, it is possible to complete the act, but never by accident.&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> &quot;From the moment of the Embrace, Caine\u2019s blood within undead veins strives toward an unholy perfection. The blood grows potent, thickening and honing in frightening and often unique ways. In addition to healing and quickening the vampire\u2019s natural strengths, vampires learn Disciplines. Disciplines focus the blood to very specific tasks, tricks, and blasphemies. For example, a Ventrue might learn Dominate, which allows her to control the minds of men, whereas a Malkavian can learn Dementation, which shatters those minds in kind.&quot;<br /> <br /> So what can we say about blood thickening? A) it about the individual never about a group or a generation, B) they say that blood thickens with <i>age</i>\u200b but surely thickens with Diablerie, C) From the moment a vampire is embraced their blood thickens and they start to learn to use their powers like Disciplines and other vampiric power. So we can see that the text seems to indicate that thickening blood is them learning to use their powers and gain new abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T17:20:50-07:00","id":1509802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1509788#post1509788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what can we say about blood thickening? A) it about the individual never about a group or a generation, B) they say that blood thickens with <i>age</i>\u200b but surely thickens with Diablerie, C) From the moment a vampire is embraced their blood thickens and they start to learn to use their powers like Disciplines and other vampiric power. So we can see that the text seems to indicate that thickening blood is them learning to use their powers and gain new abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But we have an example of this changing, and it's the only example of actual thickening without diablerie; the 15th to 16th generation. The 15th generation flaw was<br /> <br /> <b>Fifteenth Generation (4pt. Flaw)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Your vitae is so weak that only six of your 10 blood points can be used for Disciplines, healing or raising Attributes. For these functions, you must expend two blood points to obtain the effect a normal vampire would achieve with one. (The cost for nightly rising remains a single blood point.) What\u2019s more, you cannot create or sustain ghouls, create a blood bond, or <b>sire a vampiric childe</b>.</i><br /> \u200b<br /> And after a few years of them existing, it allowed them to embrace. Because the whole generation's blood thickened. And now the 16th cannot embrace. (you should eventually be able to go to 17th, with discipline dots on 1). But there's nothing showing differently. The only gen rules that seem to shift from dark to modern is that 13th generation can generally embrace. That's the blood (of the generation, not the individual) thickening.<br /> <br /> I get the experience argument, but it doesn't stand up to scrutiny. We have the Time of Thin Blood*, and it doesn't come because we have neonates, it comes because we have a lot of very weak cainites. The 13th gen were similarly weak (See the Thirteenth Generation Flaw - they get a penalty in activating disciplines) but they <b>stopped;</b> both those living for a long time, and the newly embraced ones. That doesn't fit with individual thickening, only collective.<br /> <br /> *Let me clarify here: I don't mean with have a singular time of thin blood. Thin blood comes every few generations, when the blood is too thin to properly propagate until the generation's blood collectively thickens. That said, it seems that the 17th gen should probably be the actual, no shit, Time of Thin Blood, because disciplines cannot go lower than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T06:26:24-07:00","id":1509856,"title":"","content":"But nothing you have provided proves that thickening is a mean time to happen for a generation. Again if you look at the text I provided about Thin-Blooded it states &quot;strength to do the act, physical or political&quot; which under what the other text says about thickening you can see that as the vampire ages they gain more physical power and through interacting with the world they also gain more political power allowing their offspring the ability to survive. The only reason you see this at the group level is because the majority of a generation is roughly embraced within a similar time frame.<br /> <br /> Merits and Flaws are not indicative to lore or wider mechanics. Now this may come to a shock because of how some flaws are but, even if you where to be 15th generation you don't have to have the 15th generation flaw. Likewise you don't have to be a methuselah to take Methuselah Thirst. I say this because the mechanics of what a 'thin-blood' is changes between editions and mechanical changes between editions are not necessarily indicative of lore changes. For example how Necromancy was in Dark Ages 1e was very different then the current blood sorcery that it is, this isn't a change of how necromancy as an art has progressed in character these are out of character changes to system. So has there been changes to what &quot;thin-blooded&quot; means both mechanically and lorewise? Yes it has and I'm not saying it hasn't but, those mechanical changes have no text saying they are blood thickening while the text I have provided above directly supports my statements.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T20:20:02-07:00","id":1519925,"title":"","content":"I mean, if we're disregarding all the bullshit from V5 and stick to the settings of 1e and 2e, then there may or may not be more than thirteen antediluvians but only thirteen of them actually sired. So there could very easily be a few Antediluvians who are pretty much Caitiff by default.<br /> <br /> Even Revised kinda had this as an option with one of the Gehenna scenarios, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T15:01:21-07:00","id":1520152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1519925#post1519925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if we're disregarding all the bullshit from V5 and stick to the settings of 1e and 2e, then there may or may not be more than thirteen antediluvians but only thirteen of them actually sired. So there could very easily be a few Antediluvians who are pretty much Caitiff by default.<br /> <br /> Even Revised kinda had this as an option with one of the Gehenna scenarios, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>There could be 1st, 2nd, and 3rd Generation Vampires who did not create their own Clans, but still Sired some Childe. These Childe could very own have their own attributes, preferences, abilities, tendencies, and culture.<br /> You never know, right ? Could very well be like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T20:35:06-08:00","id":1525394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1519925#post1519925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if we're disregarding all the bullshit from V5 and stick to the settings of 1e and 2e, then there may or may not be more than thirteen antediluvians but only thirteen of them actually sired. So there could very easily be a few Antediluvians who are pretty much Caitiff by default.<br /> <br /> Even Revised kinda had this as an option with one of the Gehenna scenarios, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or LESS than thirteen and some of them are just <b>very</b> good at messing with their identity and descendant inheritance through a mix of high-tier Dominate, Obfuscate &amp; Blood Magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T22:31:37-08:00","id":1525395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1525394#post1525394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or LESS than thirteen and some of them are just <b>very</b> good at messing with their identity and descendant inheritance through a mix of high-tier Dominate, Obfuscate &amp; Thaumaturgy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you, hehe.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, your ideas are intriguing and I wish to subscribe to your newsletter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T10:24:48-08:00","id":1525404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1525394#post1525394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or LESS than thirteen and some of them are just <b>very</b> good at messing with their identity and descendant inheritance through a mix of high-tier Dominate, Obfuscate &amp; Blood Magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This has already given me a handful of ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T14:33:31-08:00","id":1525410,"title":"","content":"There was Mukhtar Bey, who was a 7th Generation Caitiff and strong enough to be the Prince of Cairo for over 600 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T22:44:36-08:00","id":1525422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1525410#post1525410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was Mukhtar Bey, who was a 7th Generation Caitiff and strong enough to be the Prince of Cairo for over 600 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always wondered, who the hell Wife of the Tiger and the Snake, his sire could have been...<br /> But I guess probably a Banu Haqim... Child of Al-Ashrad (thus the Baali, sorry, Assamite Ur-Shulgi) could explain the normal look too of Mukhtar<br /> Mukhtar was a Mamluk and trained to kill as a youth<br /> And his only clan-specific discipline was Quietus<br /> Funny to immagine Mukhtar Bey as a &quot;lost&quot; assamite kid, who became Prince of Cairo<br /> <br /> Jut a thought exercise, the unknown factor of the Caitiff is part of the fun in V:tM <br /> (A kind of... easy to solve mistery via various means, for example Path of Blood. Just grab the Fledgeling and drag a Tremere or any Blood magician in, and test the blood, really<br /> Caitiff is more of a racial slur than a real condition basically and raises a very good questions of nature and nurture since you - apparently - need the long term presence of your Sire/Clan for the Clan Curse to take hold... like as if you/them <i>belive you have to be cursed </i>and &quot;make it&quot; so; it is basically really... a Mage like thing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T23:50:49-08:00","id":1525423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1525422#post1525422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just grab the Fledgeling and drag a Tremere or any Blood magician in, and test the blood, really</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the first house-rules I ported to my TT games from the LARP group I started with was that Blood Walk does not work on Caitiff. The same disconnect that prevents the childe from inheriting their sire's Disciplines and Clan Flaw also disconnects them from their bloodline. It's a bit of a hand-wave, but would explain why this isn't more common.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, this kind of makes each Caitiff a theoretical new starting point for a bloodline, but that isn't exactly lore-unfriendly either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-14T01:30:24-08:00","id":1525426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1525423#post1525423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the first house-rules I ported to my TT games from the LARP group I started with was that Blood Walk does not work on Caitiff. The same disconnect that prevents the childe from inheriting their sire's Disciplines and Clan Flaw also disconnects them from their bloodline. It's a bit of a hand-wave, but would explain why this isn't more common.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, this kind of makes each Caitiff a theoretical new starting point for a bloodline, but that isn't exactly lore-unfriendly either.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is totally logical and I used such a method...<br /> ...until Rites of Blood came out<br /> In that was described, Joseph Pander devised a ritual based on Native American initiation and manhood rites. It is known as<b> One of My Tribe</b>, and severs all metaphysical connections to sire and lineage in order to one truly &quot;become&quot; a Pander. After a vampire undergoes the ritual, she is renamed, and any powers that work through the ties of lineage can no longer target them (ex. Malkavians are even expelled from the Madness Network)<br /> So this damn ritual basically ruined that nice house rule we both used..<br /> Since it technically confirmed, no metter what, connection <i>exist</i> - and with proper method could be severed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-14T02:24:57-08:00","id":1525427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509154-an-antediluvian-caitiff?p=1525426#post1525426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is totally logical and I used such a method...<br /> ...until Rites of Blood came out<br /> In that was described, Joseph Pander devised a ritual based on Native American initiation and manhood rites. It is known as<b> One of My Tribe</b>, and severs all metaphysical connections to sire and lineage in order to one truly &quot;become&quot; a Pander. After a vampire undergoes the ritual, she is renamed, and any powers that work through the ties of lineage can no longer target them (ex. Malkavians are even expelled from the Madness Network)<br /> So this damn ritual basically ruined that nice house rule we both used..<br /> Since it technically confirmed, no metter what, connection <i>exist</i> - and with proper method could be severed</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, I have always seen this rite as a strong case in <i>support</i> of the house rule. By changing the identity of the inductee, it does two things: sever the connection to their previous bloodline, and become a Pander. If the inductee is a Caitiff to begin with, the first part just becomes forfeiting their identity as Caitiff. If the inductee is from a Clan, it only confirms that such a disconnect is possible.<br /> Would I allow a Blood Walk to succeed on a Malkavian-turned-Pander? Maybe, but more likely I would indicate to the caster that there is a magic break that prevents going back in line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-14T15:18:52-08:00","id":1525434,"title":"","content":"Mukhtar Bey as a possible member of the Banu Haqim clan is an interesting notion to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T12:17:59-08:00","id":1525469,"title":"","content":"'Caitiff' is a term that actually has two different functions, one mechanical and the other social.<br /> <br /> There's no reason that Blood Walk or a similar ability shouldn't work on someone who is a Caitiff purely in the social sense. Which is to say that they are technically a member of a Clan in a mechanical sense, having in-Clan Disciplines and a Clan weakness, but do not know their Clan or its traditions because their Sire was unwilling or unable to pass along the knowledge.<br /> <br /> How Blood Walk would work with someone like a &quot;true&quot; Caitiff or a Pander is an interesting idea to explore, and I should probably go and re-read the description of that as well as the Pander ritual to get an idea of how such a thing would work. But I do think there's an argument for the idea that while a Caitiff or Pander may no longer have a metaphysical bond to their Clan/Antediluvian, you can still track their vampiric lineage, as it were, using Blood Magic (I'll call it what I want, fight me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the question of how Caitiff are such a thing when fairly basic-level Blood Sorcery can resolve the questions of lineage and stuff, I figure there are a few pragmatic answers. The first being, who cares? It kind of doesn't matter if a magical solution to the problem exists when no one cares to apply it consistently or systemically. Certain cities might put a policy into place; others might just &quot;solve&quot; the problem with a Scourge.<br /> <br /> Meaning that using Blood Walk to resolve an issue of lineage is largely a personal problem for the Caitiff in question. Taking action to resolve said problem then involves a few necessary steps:<br /> <br /> 1) Finding out the solution exists. An implicit part of the problem for &quot;social&quot; Caitiff is that no one bothered to teach them this stuff in the first place, so they aren't necessarily going to be aware that there is an arcane solution to their problem.<br /> <br /> 2) Finding someone with the necessary abilities. While the Path of Blood is pretty common, Blood Walk is a separate ritual. And while practitioners of Blood Magic aren't *too* rare, they aren't super common either, so there's a limited pool of potential helpers.<br /> <br /> 3) Trusting a freaking Blood Sorcerer with your Vitae! This applies especially to the Tremere, who are pretty well-known for using the &quot;undesirables&quot; of Kindred society as guinea pigs, but I'd say it holds up in general. Vampires are assholes, and Blood Mages are no exception. My mind always goes to the conversation in BJD where Vykos is grateful that their discarded bits are being used as a trophy rather than winding up in the hands of the Tremere. Just because you give a Tremere a sample of your Vitae for the purposes of checking your lineage, that doesn't mean they'll *only* use it for that, or even that they will honour the agreement in the first place.<br /> <br /> So getting the answers can be difficult, and even dangerous, for the Caitiff in question. But even if they did get the answer, what good would it do them? A lot of Kindred don't really care that much about their Clan as a whole, so being able to tell someone that you're from the same Clan isn't going to guarantee much. It doesn't change the fact that the Caitiff doesn't really know anything, and teaching them is a *burden* that their own Sire already opted out of, so why would someone else bother?<br /> <br /> Even in the cases of high-profile and powerful Caitiff, like Mukhtar Bey, if they do have a lineage/Clan to discover, it never helped them before, so why bother trying to figure it out now? A Caitiff that reaches that level has already managed to climb the ladder without the benefits of a known Clan, so why make a big deal out of it now? That doesn't even go into the possibility of taking pride in Caitiff status, as the Panders do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}